<article class="env-lemma" id="036K">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/036K">Lemma <span data-tag="036K">35.27.1</span>.</a> The property $\mathcal{P}(f)=$“$f$ is flat” is fpqc local on the source. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Since flatness is defined in terms of the maps of local rings (Morphisms, Definition <a href="/tag/01U3" data-tag="01U3">29.26.1</a>) what has to be shown is the following algebraic fact: Suppose $A \to B \to C$ are local homomorphisms of local rings, and assume $B \to C$ is flat. Then $A \to B$ is flat if and only if $A \to C$ is flat. If $A \to B$ is flat, then $A \to C$ is flat by Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00HC" data-tag="00HC">10.39.4</a>. Conversely, assume $A \to C$ is flat. Note that $B \to C$ is faithfully flat, see Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00HR" data-tag="00HR">10.39.17</a>. Hence $A \to B$ is flat by Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/039V" data-tag="039V">10.39.10</a>. (Also see Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/02JZ" data-tag="02JZ">29.26.13</a> for a direct proof.) 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>